.TH CHTTPSVR_SET_ENGINE_NUM_REACTOR_THREADS 3 "2026-07-17" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_set_engine_num_reactor_threads \- set the OS thread count for the shared engine's reactor
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_set_engine_num_reactor_threads(size_t num_threads);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Configures how many OS threads the shared event_loop reactor devotes
to its own polling and dispatch, per event_loop_create_with_mprocs's
own num_reactor_threads parameter (see cthreadcomm.h): 1 means a
single thread both polls and dispatches inline; any larger value means
one dedicated polling thread plus (num_threads - 1) dispatch worker
threads.

By default (never having called this function, or having called it
with num_threads == 0), the reactor sizes itself to
sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN), falling back to 1 if that query fails.
Passing a positive num_threads overrides that auto-detection and pins
the reactor to exactly that many threads instead; passing 0 restores
the default auto-detected sizing.

Like chttpsvr_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs, this configures a value baked
into the reactor at construction time: it may only be called before
the first chttpsvr_start call in the process, or again after the
reactor has fully stopped (chttpsvr_engine_wait has returned), before
the next chttpsvr_start.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
ccol_not_permitted if the reactor is already running; stop it first.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs (3),
.BR chttpsvr_set_engine_logger (3),
.BR chttpsvr_start (3),
.BR chttpsvr_engine_stop (3),
.BR chttpsvr_engine_wait (3),
.BR chttpcli_set_engine_num_reactor_threads (3)
